## Best Practices

### 1. ViewModel Guidelines
- ViewModels should not reference View types
- Use interfaces for view interactions
- Keep business logic out of ViewModels (use services)
- Implement INotifyPropertyChanged properly
- Use CallerMemberName for OnPropertyChanged

### 2. View Guidelines
- Minimize code-behind (use ViewModels)
- Use data binding over code
- Separate concerns (View for UI, ViewModel for logic)
- Use UserControls for reusable components

### 3. Data Binding
- Always use `{Binding}` syntax
- Specify `UpdateSourceTrigger` when needed
- Use `StringFormat` for simple formatting
- Prefer converters over code-behind

### 4. Commands
- Use ICommand for all user actions
- Keep commands simple and focused
- Handle CanExecute properly
- Use async commands for long operations

### 5. Performance
- Use virtualization for large lists
- Lazy-load data when possible
- Avoid heavy operations on UI thread
- Profile and optimize rendering

### 6. Error Handling
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for debugging
- Provide recovery options
- Don't crash on errors

### 7. Accessibility
- Provide keyboard shortcuts
- Support tab navigation
- Use proper ARIA labels
- Test with screen readers

### 8. Cross-Platform Considerations
- Test on Windows, macOS, Linux
- Use platform-agnostic paths
- Handle platform-specific features gracefully
- Use Avalonia's platform detection

## XAML Best Practices

### Layout
```xml
<!-- Good: Clear hierarchy -->
<Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
    <Menu Grid.Row="0"/>
    <ContentControl Grid.Row="1" Content="{Binding CurrentView}"/>
    <StatusBar Grid.Row="2"/>
</Grid>

<!-- Bad: Nested absolute positioning -->
<Canvas>
    <Canvas Canvas.Left="10" Canvas.Top="10">
        <Button Content="Click"/>
    </Canvas>
</Canvas>
```

### Naming
```xml
<!-- Good: Descriptive names -->
<Button x:Name="OpenProjectButton" Content="Open Project"/>

<!-- Bad: Generic names -->
<Button x:Name="Button1" Content="Open Project"/>
```

### Resources
```xml
<!-- Good: Reusable resources -->
<Window.Resources>
    <Style x:Key="HeaderTextStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="24"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold"/>
    </Style>
</Window.Resources>

<TextBlock Style="{StaticResource HeaderTextStyle}" Text="Header"/>
```

## Testing Strategy
- Unit test ViewModels (no UI dependencies)
- Test commands independently
- Test converters with various inputs
- Integration tests with Avalonia test framework
- UI automation tests for critical paths

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- Don't put business logic in code-behind
- Avoid tight coupling between Views and ViewModels
- Don't block UI thread with long operations
- Avoid massive ViewModels (split into smaller ones)
- Don't duplicate SDK logic in GUI
- Avoid memory leaks (unsubscribe from events)
- Don't ignore cross-platform differences
